							<p style="MARGIN: 12pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: 121%"><font color="#d3d3d3"><b><i><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-family: Arial"><font color="#d3d3d3">History of Apostle&nbsp;Masterfu Mushuru</font>&nbsp;<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /><o:p></o:p></span></i></b></font></p> <p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 12pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 121%"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#d3d3d3">Long, long ago, in a place not so very far away, a very important lizard-child was brought into this world. You may know him now as the wise and powerful, Apostle Masterfu Mushuru. However, he was not always known by this name. His exact age is not known, as his past is unclear up until the past 5 years or so, but rest assured he as been growing in knowledge and power since the day he was born to his well known Iksar parents. When his father Glox met his mother Niska many years ago as fledgling monks studying in the footsteps of the great god Cazic Thule, they had no idea what fate would hold in store for them. See back then, Glox and Niska were both young themselves, but neither of them were without power in their family tree. Glox is a direct descendant of the monk Eejag, the fist of Fire, and Niska is the sister of the mother of another wondrous monk, well known to many simply as Veltar. Thus you can see how Masterfu was born with not only strong parents to raise him with the ways of martial arts governing his future, but he also has very powerful and potent blood flowing through his veins from not just one, but both sides of the family. <o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 12pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 121%"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#d3d3d3">As the years passed Glox and Niska grew closer to one another, and eventually fell in love. Shortly after their romance was established they were both promoted to the rank of Master in the Court of Pain… the ancient order of monk-hood in charge of training future monks for the defense of the great city of Cabilis. Shortly thereafter Masterfu was born. He spent his younger years training long and hard with his parents and the other masters of the court, so that one day he would be strong, powerful, and be able to take over the legacy of Glox and Niska. <o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 12pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 121%"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#d3d3d3">During his adolescent years he disappeared from existence as his parents took and put him on a ship and sent him to the great expansive waters of the ocean known more commonly as Timorous Deep. He spent many, many years here studying under the tutelage of Master Rinmark, one of the most powerful monks still alive today. He is as wise as he is old, yet still very remarkable in his ability, and during his stay with Rinmark, Masterfu learned much of his skills and abilities, and even took on a bit of his gruff demeanor. After reaching maturity and learning all he could from Master Rinmark, Masterfu returned home to Cabilis to discover that his father had taken over in the stead of the previous head of the Court of Pain and was now the senior in charge, still known as Grand Master Glox today. His mother, Niska is the highest ranking Master below her husband. Needless to say Masterfu’s parents were delighted at all he had learned from Master Rinmark, for in fact, while he was away studying and practicing, he had become even more powerful than his parents. <o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 12pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 121%"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#d3d3d3">Masterfu spent a number of years assisting his parents in the running of the Court of Pain, and the defense of the great Iksar city… until recently that is, when he decided it was time for another adventure, and that is where he resurfaces and is recorded in the history books of the common tongue, but that was only within the past 5 years. Masterfu left Cabilis and journeyed around the world of Norrath, meeting many new people, forging friendships, and defeating vile beats in the name of Cazic Thule. <o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 12pt; TEXT-INDENT: 0.5in; LINE-HEIGHT: 121%"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'"><font color="#d3d3d3">Then just a few years ago Masterfu learned of several relics that bestowed upon the wielder, great power beyond belief. So he gathered the necessary information and embarked to attain these two artifacts. First was the Whistling Fists, a great weapon, which after a long hard road, through the Dreadlands of Kunark, where he met his cousin Veltar, the ruins of old Sebilis, and even into the realm of his great god, the Plane of Fear… he was finally bestowed with the honor and power of the Whistling Fists by Cazic Thule himself. With one of the artifacts down, he sought the other, even more powerful artifact, the Celestial Fists. This artifact, though not requiring as much time, was harder to acquire by ten fold. It took him through the Plane of Sky, through the great mines of Nurga, and pitted him against the 4 great monk masters of the past, including the ghost of his ancestor Eejag the fist of Fire. But finally, after defeating the fowl demon Xenovorash, he returned the demon’s fangs to the monk currently caring for the awesome Celestial Fists, upon which he was granted the right to be their next bearer. Having achieved the final rung of skill in both the orders of the Whistling and Celestial Fists, Masterfu is considered by many to be one of the most powerful monks alive in Norrath today. <o:p></o:p></font></span></p> <p><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><font color="#d3d3d3">His parents Grandmaster Glox and Master Niska, can still be found in Cabilis as they still run the Court of Pain there. His ancestor Eejag’s ghost, can still be found swimming in the molten hot magma of the Lavastorm Mountains, and his cousin Veltar still wanders around Karnor’s Castle in the Dreadlands of Kunark. Masterfu has come to be an advisor of the great queen Amyana of the guild Moonlite Redemption, and he is one of her most trusted advisors and confidantes. Together with the other strong officers of Moonlite Redemption, they continue to lead the guild to bigger and better things, and work towards many great goals and ideals, that they all share in common, the most important of these being family.</font></span></p> <p align="center"><span style="FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333333; FONT-FAMILY: QuillScript; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; mso-fareast-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-bidi-font-family: 'Times New Roman'; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA"><font color="#d3d3d3"></font></span>&nbsp;</p> <p align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v511/Amyana/Hierachy/fu.jpg" /> </font></p><br /> <p align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v511/Amyana/Hierachy/MasterfuMushuru2.jpg" /> </font></p><br /> <p align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v511/Amyana/Hierachy/niska.jpg" /></font></p><br /> <p align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v511/Amyana/Hierachy/glox.jpg" /></font></p> <p align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v511/Amyana/Hierachy/eejag.jpg" /></font></p> <p align="center"><font color="#d3d3d3"><img src="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v511/Amyana/Hierachy/veltar.jpg" /></font></p>
							
